===1974 to present===
All Ohio passenger plates issued since October 2001 are valid for display today, provided they have been continuously registered. "Ohio Gold" plates, issued from August 1996 through September 2001, were replaced during 2022 due to readability issues arising from degradation of the reflective sheeting through exposure to humidity, rain, snow, and road salt.<ref>{{cite web |last=Schupp |first=Kim |date=November 10, 2021 |title=Got an 'Ohio Gold' license plate? The BMV says it has to be replaced |url=https://www.fox19.com/2021/11/10/got-an-ohio-gold-license-plate-bmv-says-it-has-be-replaced/ |publisher=[[WXIX-TV]] |access-date=January 23, 2022}}</ref>
