==Temporary tags== 
Vehicles purchased from a dealership are given a 30-day or 45-day temporary tag. The paper tag is filled out by hand. Since March 2001, it has featured a hologram.<ref name="Temp tag notice">{{cite web|title=Issuing Requirements|publisher=Dealer Licensing Division, [[Ohio Bureau of Motor Vehicles]]|date=2009-12-01|access-date=2010-09-19|url=http://www.bmv.ohio.gov/dealer_licensing/temp-tag-training.htm|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100719180002/http://bmv.ohio.gov/dealer_licensing/temp-tag-training.htm|archive-date=2010-07-19|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="ODPS history">{{cite web|title=ODPS Ohio Bureau of Motor Vehicles History|publisher=Ohio Bureau of Motor Vehicles|access-date=2010-09-19|url=http://www.bmv.ohio.gov/history.stm|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140714194533/http://www.bmv.ohio.gov/history.stm|archive-date=2014-07-14|url-status=dead}}</ref> On a 2001-series temporary tag, the plate number is preprinted, while the expiration date and vehicle details are written in permanent marker. As of August, 2020, the Ohio Department of Public Safety issues print-on-demand temporary tags and will phase out traditional paper tags in January 2021.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://publicsafety.ohio.gov/wps/portal/gov/odps/news-and-events/all-news/bmv_08202020 |title=New Print-On-Demand Dealer Tag Available |website=publicsafety.ohio.gov |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201005070431/https://publicsafety.ohio.gov/wps/portal/gov/odps/news-and-events/all-news/bmv_08202020 |archive-date=2020-10-05}} </ref>

