==County coding==
In 1992, Ohio began using a numerical county-coding scheme to indicate the [[List of counties in Ohio|county of registration]]. The scheme assigns a two-digit number to each of the state's 88 counties in alphabetical order, beginning with 01 for [[Adams County, Ohio|Adams County]] and ending with 88 for [[Wyandot County, Ohio|Wyandot County]]. The scheme has been used on specialty plates since its introduction, and was also used on standard passenger plates from 2001 until 2018.

The county number is displayed on red or white stickers placed at the bottom left corner the plate. The stickers also display the county name, in small print below the number.

